WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.230
The Purge: Election Year offered up a rather
conclusive ending to James DeMonaco's dystopian

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.361
film trilogy, but he still isn't done scaring
the pants off anyone with a finger on the

00:00:09.361 --> 00:00:11.050
political pulse just yet.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.900
For its fourth outing, The Purge series is
heading back in time to the very first Purge

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.440
event staged by the New Founding Fathers of
America to show how such a brutal holiday

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.720
became a part of society to begin with.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.369
The First Purge will arrive in theaters on
Independence Day 2018, and the film is expected

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:30.930
to be very direct with its real-life socio-political
parallels while still offering a bloody good

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.230
time at the theater.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.629
Here's what you need to know about The First
Purge before heading out for the next round

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:37.219
of mayhem.

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:38.839
Contained mayhem

00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:43.280
Whereas the original Purge trilogy took place
long after the annual night of terror overtook

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.499
the entire United States, The First Purge
will focus solely on Staten Island in New

00:00:47.499 --> 00:00:48.499
York.

00:00:48.499 --> 00:00:51.690
That setting has been chosen to serve as the
host of the inaugural evening of violence,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:56.030
at a time when people are still unprepared
for the levels of depravity it will unleash.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:59.209
From the trailers, it is clear that certain
members of the neighborhood will stand in

00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:01.659
vocal resistance to the concept of the Purge.

00:01:01.659 --> 00:01:05.030
However, as we already know from the first
three films, their efforts will ultimately

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.450
fail to stop the spread of violence and in
fact, the efforts of the marginalized to demand

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:13.450
justice might just be part of the reason the
tradition takes hold of the rest of the nation

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.469
in the first place.

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:17.780
"Your government thanks you for your participation."

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:19.560
Spectator sport

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.210
In the film, we'll meet the woman who creates
the experimental night of lawlessness, and

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.979
she seems to think her terrible test is going
to satisfy the bloodlust of everybody in America.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:32.219
"If we want to save our country we must release
all our anger in one night."

00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:35.969
However, many of this Purge's participants
will have to be bribed into sticking around,

00:01:35.969 --> 00:01:39.640
which means most of them are from a very vulnerable
sector of society.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.990
As DeMonaco told Vulture:

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:45.189
"What they do is start promising very decent
sums of money for the very poor people in

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:46.189
the neighborhood.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.920
It becomes a monetization of murder and violence,
incentivizing killing and keeping people around

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.189
for them to be victims."

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:56.090
The trailer also hints that ex-military members
will be hired to enter the experiment and

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.899
slaughter people to help amplify the entertainment
for audiences tuning in.

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:04.020
So, there might not be enough people itching
to maim each other before the big guns start

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.999
stepping in.

00:02:05.999 --> 00:02:06.999
Real-life parallels

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:12.860
In 2016's Election Year, there were some unintentional,
albeit eerie, overlaps with current events,

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.580
including the similarities between Donald
Trump's "Make America Great Again" campaign

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.810
slogan and the film's own "Keep America Great"
tagline.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.110
With The First Purge, however, the parallels
are no longer accidental.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:27.290
The first poster made that clear from the
start, depicting a simple red ball cap bearing

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:31.209
the film's title and a striking resemblance
to Trump's signature hats.

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:36.040
The movie is also expected to use similar
language and cultural anxieties as those related

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:40.720
to the current administration, including having
one of the key motives of the NFFA being "a

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.909
dying economy."

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:43.560
Sound familiar?

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.129
Surprising inspiration

00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:49.879
Frank Grillo's Leo Barnes, also known as "The
Sergeant," and Edwin Hodge's Dante Bishop

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:54.129
may have arrived as hesitant heroes over the
course of the first three Purge films.

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:57.590
But this time around, DeMonaco isn't pulling
any punches when it comes to who's leading

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:58.590
the good guys.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.940
Y'lan Noel's character, William, is shown
in the trailer gathering the neighborhood

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.750
troops to rebel against the Purge - and he
seems to have some well-developed fighting

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.750
skills.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.590
According to DeMonaco, the character is an
anti-hero who was originally inspired by Clint

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.209
Eastwood's role in Unforgiven: Will Munny.

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:17.500
Munny was a former assassin who was recruited
to serve up some vigilante justice and proved

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.720
to be effective at taking lives, so we should
expect some pretty badass fight scenes ahead.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.370
Fresh blood

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.060
DeMonaco wrote and directed all three of the
original Purge films, but this time, he's

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.400
taking a back seat to allow a new director
to guide the franchise.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.370
The script is still his creation, but The
First Purge is being helmed by relative newcomer

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:39.560
Gerard McMurray, whose Sundance debut Burning
Sands caught DeMonaco's eye.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.469
It was one of McMurray's real-life experiences
that helped him get the gig, though.

00:03:43.469 --> 00:03:44.819
As DeMonaco told Vulture:

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:48.989
"He lived through [Hurricane] Katrina, and
Katrina was one of the early influences on

00:03:48.989 --> 00:03:53.060
The Purge itself when I saw the treatment
of the people in the Ninth Ward by the government.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.920
[…] So we met with Gerard, it was just the
perfect fit."

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.860
Even before hiring McMurray, DeMonaco knew
he wanted to feature a predominantly black

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.930
cast in the film, as it's been important to
him since the second installment to put people

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.909
of color at the center of his films.

00:04:05.909 --> 00:04:06.909
As he explained:

00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:10.420
"We always talk about how the only way to
change the system is to make successful things

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.050
with a black lead or female lead.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.360
It's the only way to do it.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:16.430
At first we were saying, it's not a race movie,
it's more about class.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:18.330
But ultimately race is class."

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:22.950
The subject of socioeconomic disparity seems
to be front and center of the newest Purge

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:26.410
film, but for those who aren't so interested
in the message, the film might still be for

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.350
you because…

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.850
Thrills and chills

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.720
There's no doubt that DeMonaco and the rest
of The First Purge's creators made a movie

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.250
with a political point.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:40.000
Even the inclusion of real-life CNN host Van
Jones on the cast makes for a very meta moment

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.020
of questioning the tactics of government.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:46.940
However, for those who've tuned out the 24-hour
news cycle and want a plain old popcorn-and-gore

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.780
theatrical experience, there's plenty of that
as well.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.780
As DeMonaco promised:

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.250
"The people who want to can see the parallels
to our society and the reflection upon our

00:04:55.250 --> 00:05:00.030
government and talk about that after the movie,
or they can watch it as just a real fun, kick-ass

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:01.040
action-horror film."

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:05.250
So, it sounds like there'll be a little something
scary for everyone when The First Purge lands

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.290
in theaters this July 4th, 2018.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.390
Thanks for watching!

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:11.530
